WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:04.250
Magic, killer clowns, and the actual grim
reaper?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.753
The ending of "Twisted Metal" hinted at a
lot of possibilities.

00:00:07.753 --> 00:00:11.889
Here's what might be coming down the road
in a possible second season.

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:17.700
John Doe is a "milkman," essentially an extremely
skilled driver with a souped-up and weaponized

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.310
car, who couriers goods, such as medicine,
food, and other supplies, across the post-apocalyptic

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.029
world of the "Divided States of America."

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:31.651
John also has amnesia, with only a burnt photo
of him as a kid to link him to his past.

00:00:31.651 --> 00:00:37.290
It's eventually revealed in Episode 3 that
the world ended in the year 2002 after a Y2K-type

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.764
event decimated everything all over the world.

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:45.090
Walled cities were constructed to protect
the affluent from the dangerous outside world

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.012
of scavenging and violence.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:52.370
One such city is New San Francisco — run
by the power-hungry mayor Raven — a place

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.160
John does milkman runs for.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.384
The story of "Twisted Metal" gets going when
Raven offers John a job he can't pass up.

00:00:59.384 --> 00:01:04.470
"If you go to New Chicago and bring this package
back for me, I will make you a citizen of

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.164
New San Francisco."

00:01:06.164 --> 00:01:07.703
"I get to live here?"

00:01:07.703 --> 00:01:12.070
John has ten days to complete his mission,
but things get complicated when he gets carjacked

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.035
by Quiet.

00:01:13.035 --> 00:01:18.638
She's a fugitive on the run from Agent Stone,
who leads a dangerous gang of would-be police officers.

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:23.119
While John and Quiet are antagonistic towards
each other at first, they eventually learn

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:27.900
to work together, and even fall in love, over
the course of their violent road trip.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.530
At the end of "Twisted Metal," John Doe completes
Raven's mission and delivers the package from

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.900
New Chicago to New San Francisco at the last
minute.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.630
He's looking forward to having a safe place
to live behind the city walls, but his new

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.492
partner throws a wrench in the plan.

00:01:41.492 --> 00:01:43.839
Quiet isn't allowed inside.

00:01:43.839 --> 00:01:48.220
"We had a deal, John.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.082
You and me."

00:01:49.082 --> 00:01:51.785
"And she's with me, that's all you need to
know."

00:01:51.785 --> 00:01:55.909
Before John has the chance to reject the offer
of salvation in New San Francisco to stay

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:57.810
with Quiet, she shoots him.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:03.457
The violent act is done out of love so John
can be taken into medical care by the NSF medics.

00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:08.190
John is content in NSF for a while, but he
becomes bored by the repetitive routine of

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.862
the suburban-like existence of the walled-in
city.

00:02:10.862 --> 00:02:15.360
When he tells Raven his plans to leave NSF
and find Quiet, she tries to convince him

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.000
to stay by revealing his family was from Old
San Francisco before the apocalypse.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.530
John still insists on leaving, but Raven doesn't
take the rejection well.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:29.130
It's at this point that she reveals her real
plan: she sent John out to test his driving

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:33.582
before forcing him to represent her in an
upcoming contest.

00:02:33.582 --> 00:02:37.063
Before Quiet joined John on his mission, she
had a quest of her own.

00:02:37.063 --> 00:02:41.280
At the beginning of the season, Quiet's brother
Loud kills himself rather than let his sister

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.140
die at the hands of Agent Stone, the leader
of a gang of cops trying to "restore order"

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.800
in the post-apocalyptic Divided States of
America.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.860
However, rather than restoring order, they
spread terror, violence, and fear, including

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:58.200
turning the DMV into a Guantanamo Bay-esque
torture black site.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.170
Though she helps John on his drive, Quiet
never stops hunting for Stone, and John's

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.892
involvement complicates things.

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:08.500
The loss of Quiet's brother left her hopeless
and with a death wish, but John's friendship,

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.162
and later love, make her realize that she
could find new connections.

00:03:12.162 --> 00:03:16.522
In the end, instead of killing Stone in cold
blood after beating him in car combat, she

00:03:16.522 --> 00:03:19.785
decides to wash her hands of him and move
on to heal.

00:03:19.785 --> 00:03:24.370
After she leaves John, Quiet, going by the
codename "Roadkill," becomes a liberator of

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.252
the wasteland.

00:03:25.252 --> 00:03:29.860
She steals and hijacks supplies from wayward
milkmen to give back to the homeless and needy

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.560
in a Robin Hood sort of way.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.374
Eventually, though, she's caught by the Dollface
gang whose leader turns out to be John's long-lost sister.

00:03:37.374 --> 00:03:41.799
While not one of the main characters, Stu
is still important in the "Twisted Metal" series.

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:45.890
He and his friend Mike are based on the characters
in "Twisted Metal 2" who drive the monster

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:49.409
truck Hammerhead, which sadly doesn't make
an appearance this season.

00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:53.860
In the show, rather than being metalhead stoners
who wish for the ability to fly, Mike and

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:59.918
Stu are wayward scavengers, about to be eaten
by cannibals before being saved by Agent Stone's goons.

00:03:59.918 --> 00:04:04.360
Stone then offers Mike and Stu the opportunity
to be law-bringers like them.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:09.096
Stu, however, realizes very quickly that he's
not cruel enough to be a law-bringer, and

00:04:09.096 --> 00:04:11.200
Mike eventually sells him out.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.420
Luckily, before Stu is executed, he's rescued
by Sweet Tooth.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.350
The evil clown takes a quick liking to Stu,
partially due to them being big dudes whose

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.970
first names start with "s."

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:26.690
Unfortunately, while Sweet Tooth is supportive
of Stu, he's also psychotic and manipulative,

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:32.004
and at one point during the final battle against
Stone kills some allies with no remorse.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:35.133
"There are no sides, Stubert.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.603
Everybody burns."

00:04:36.603 --> 00:04:41.259
When Sweet Tooth forces Stu to kill Mike,
Stu refuses, standing up for himself, and

00:04:41.259 --> 00:04:43.123
shooting Sweet Tooth in the eye.

00:04:43.123 --> 00:04:47.479
Fans of the game will recognize that this
gives the clown his iconic video game injury

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:49.677
from "Twisted Metal: Black."

00:04:49.677 --> 00:04:54.110
Like so much television and film these days,
there is, of course, an after credits scene

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.690
following the ending of the "Twisted Metal"
finale.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.980
We see Mike and Stu enjoying their time together
on a secluded beach with their "girlfriends,"

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.903
but they're interrupted by an unexpected visitor.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:04.470
"Good evening!"

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.470
"Oh, s—!"

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:09.169
"Actually, I have a better idea."

00:05:09.169 --> 00:05:13.560
Mike and Stu share a nervous laugh with Sweet
Tooth, but they're terrified — after all,

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:17.060
the last time they saw the violent clown,
they hit him with their van.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.759
Unfortunately for them, Sweet Tooth stops
laughing, takes out a machete, and stabs Mike

00:05:21.759 --> 00:05:22.602
to death.

00:05:22.602 --> 00:05:25.183
Afterward, Sweet Tooth drags Stu away screaming.

00:05:25.183 --> 00:05:26.973
Is Mike actually dead?

00:05:26.973 --> 00:05:31.920
If so, does it end the potential of seeing
Mike and Stu drive a monster truck together?

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.121
While that could indeed be true, the whole
thing could be a fake-out.

00:05:35.121 --> 00:05:39.401
Maybe Mike survives his wounds, or maybe it's
the setup to an elaborate joke.

00:05:39.401 --> 00:05:43.539
It would definitely be nice to see Mike return
— it would be a pretty big disappointment

00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:48.030
to see Hammerhead on screen without both Mike
and Stu behind the wheel.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.780
The "Twisted Metal" series isn't subtle about
its anti-capitalist nature.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:56.570
It shows the great disparity between the haves
and have-nots in the new post-apocalyptic

00:05:56.570 --> 00:06:01.199
society, and how those in power will always
continue to amass more wealth and resources

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:03.163
by exploiting those in poverty.

00:06:03.163 --> 00:06:08.031
This is made pretty clear by the walled-in
cities of New San Francisco or New Chicago.

00:06:08.031 --> 00:06:12.841
In these cities, a small minority of affluent
people live in opulence and luxury, while

00:06:12.841 --> 00:06:15.898
the majority of the world lives in poverty
and squalor.

00:06:15.898 --> 00:06:18.280
However, the critique goes beyond that.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.645
Consider Quiet's backstory set in the walled
city of Orange County.

00:06:21.645 --> 00:06:26.420
After the end of the world, the OC became
a fascistic nightmare, where white upper-middle

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:31.780
class and suburban-coded denizens keep marginalized
and minority workers as slaves.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.690
Though not a true reflection of the actual
place, there is no question that our world

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:40.250
has a long and sad history of subjugating
citizens for the benefit of a few wealthy

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.276
and powerful people.

00:06:42.276 --> 00:06:47.009
Another important message of "Twisted Metal"
is the necessity of human connections, bonds,

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:48.080
and community.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:53.039
In capitalism, everything is set up as a competition,
and relationships within that system are meant

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:54.764
to be seen as transactional.

00:06:54.764 --> 00:06:59.290
Even personal friendships under capitalism
are often viewed as merely stepping stones

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:03.919
for people to network and elevate their careers
— always at the expense of others.

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:07.740
We see how this manifests at the beginning
of the show, when John Doe's only friend is

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.240
his car, Evelyn.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.970
The same goes for Quiet, who isolates herself
from human connection by not even speaking.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:18.280
They both work alone in their own little toxic
bubbles — and even when they're forced together

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.790
due to unforeseen circumstances, they still
try to find ways to undermine or exploit each

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.294
other at every opportunity.

00:07:24.294 --> 00:07:28.380
Once they decide to actually open up to each
other and work together as a team, they start

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.697
to actually succeed in ways they couldn't
have if they were alone.

00:07:31.697 --> 00:07:35.560
They even find love and a bond that their
isolation denied them.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.680
It's this connection to others that even leads
to Quiet becoming a liberator for the people

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.440
of the wasteland: she is attempting to foster
communities by providing them basic necessities

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.030
denied by their world.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:51.449
In an interview with SyFy, Samoa Joe said
he hopes that the second season gets to be

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:53.270
more violent and dark.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:57.090
In the first season of "Twisted Metal," Sweet
Tooth is far less bloodthirsty and evil than

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.169
he is in the games.

00:07:58.169 --> 00:08:02.810
He is indeed violent and psychotic, but there's
a silliness to Joe and Will Arnett's portrayal

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.710
of the evil clown that's absent from the games.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.250
This is especially true for the later games
on which the show is based.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.639
In an interview with Deadline, Anthony Mackie
said,

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:15.550
"[John]'s going to have some challenges that's
gonna come his way that's gonna force his

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:19.300
hand to be more of an adult and make some
really tough decisions because you can't be

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.000
a milkman all your life."

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:26.590
It seems that there are going to be many morally
gray moments in Season 2 if it indeed happens.

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:31.520
If Twister, Quiet, or even his sister Dollface
joins the tournament, and it's "kill or be

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.399
killed," how do you make the right choice
of who lives or dies?

00:08:35.399 --> 00:08:39.390
One of the most exciting aspects of the ending
of "Twisted Metal" season one is the fact

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:43.459
that it actually introduces the Twisted Metal
contest into the story.

00:08:43.459 --> 00:08:47.640
Much like the 2021 "Mortal Kombat" movie,
the 2023 "Twisted Metal" streaming series

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.900
doesn't even introduce the main event that
the whole thing is named after — we'll just

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.620
have to wait for more episodes to continue
the story.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.410
To hold over die-hard fans, there are glimpses
of other drivers from the game — including

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.864
fan-favorites Mr. Grimm and Axel.

00:09:00.864 --> 00:09:05.160
They also imply that other drivers from the
game who showed up earlier in the series — like

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:09.683
Twister, Preacher, and Flower Power — will
be joining the Twisted Metal tournament as well.

00:09:09.683 --> 00:09:13.769
Raven is a playable character in the 2001
game "Twisted Metal: Black" — and while

00:09:13.769 --> 00:09:17.339
the two characters have nothing in common,
it's certainly possible that we could see

00:09:17.339 --> 00:09:19.212
the show's version behind the wheel.

00:09:19.212 --> 00:09:23.780
Finally, there's also the possibility that
Agent Stone survived the finale — after

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.834
all, we don't see him die on-screen.

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.252
Could his character be joining the tournament
also?

00:09:28.252 --> 00:09:31.012
We'll just have to wait and see.

00:09:31.012 --> 00:09:35.570
Another exciting thing about the end of Season
1 is that it could also lead to the introduction

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:38.260
of the supernatural elements that exist in
the game.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.959
While John and Quiet hear Calypso's voice
while picking up Raven's package in New Chicago,

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:46.931
he's not really mentioned in the show outside
of some shots of graffiti saying "Calypso

00:09:46.931 --> 00:09:48.163
is Real" and such.

00:09:48.163 --> 00:09:52.540
However, in the games, Calypso is the one
who runs the Twisted Metal tournament in nearly

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:57.060
every entry, and he has magical powers that
grant any wish the winner of the tournament

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:01.170
desires — though the wish usually backfires
in a Monkey's Paw sort of way.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:05.850
In the finale, once Raven forces John at gunpoint
to be her driver in the Twisted Metal tournament,

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.820
she hints at a big reward.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:12.410
"I need you to win, because Calypso is offering
quite the prize.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:14.640
The winner gets their heart's desire.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.373
Their greatest wish come true."

00:10:17.373 --> 00:10:20.582
This might mean that Calypso has magic powers
in the show as well.

00:10:20.582 --> 00:10:24.600
This also means that Mr. Grimm — who is
briefly seen in one of the photos during the

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:29.450
montage of contestants — could be the actual
Grim Reaper like he was in the first two games.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:33.660
He's been human in other games, but the Reaper
version is still a fan favorite.

